{
  "evals": [
    {
      "id": "bundle-preflight-stage0",
      "prompt": "Before I book the allocation for the eight-process Stage 0 launch of Sim-Bimanual, check on this single-GPU machine that the training data loads. Use the versioned single-source robot example that the nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual checkpoint publishes on Hugging Face under examples/training as the training bundle: download it, verify its checksum and extract it with the commands its README records (the example is not bundled in the skill). Bind the extracted bundle and run the skill's two data checks on it: the static bundle check, then the check that reads one packed Stage 0 sample through the native loader. These checks do not load model weights, so do not download Cosmos3-Nano or the video VAE and do not launch training. Use the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill (public repository https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git), as the framework checkout and set up its training environment as the skill documents. Save the unmodified standard output of the static check as outputs/bundle_static_check.json and of the Stage 0 check as outputs/bundle_materialize_stage0.json, and record the reported sample and token counts and the tensor shapes and dtypes in result_summary.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "Both data checks pass on the published single-source robot example from the Framework training environment: the static check reports passed: true and materialized: false, the Stage 0 check reports passed: true and materialized: true with the batch sample and token counts and tensor shapes and dtypes, the two reports are saved as outputs/bundle_static_check.json and outputs/bundle_materialize_stage0.json, and result_summary.md records the commands and the reported values.",
      "assertions": [
        "The training bundle is the single-source robot example downloaded from examples/training of nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual on Hugging Face, checksum-verified and extracted with the commands the example's README records, not a substitute or hand-made bundle",
        "Both checks ran from the Framework training environment the skill documents (Python 3.13, the cu130-train or cu128-train group matching the host and the train extra; not the system python), in the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill",
        "python -m cosmos_framework.scripts.validate_bimanual_data --bundle ran on the extracted bundle, the path the skill binds as COSMOS_SIM_BIMANUAL_LOCAL_BUNDLE; outputs/bundle_static_check.json is that command's unmodified standard output and reports passed: true and materialized: false",
        "python -m cosmos_framework.scripts.validate_bimanual_data --bundle with --materialize --stage 0 ran on the same bundle; outputs/bundle_materialize_stage0.json is that command's unmodified standard output and reports passed: true and materialized: true with the batch sample and token counts and tensor shapes and dtypes",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: both reports trace to real command runs in the transcript, no model weights were downloaded or loaded for these checks, and result_summary.md records the exact commands, their wall time and the values actually reported"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/bundle_static_check.json",
          "min_bytes": 40,
          "contains": "\"passed\": true"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/bundle_static_check.json",
          "min_bytes": 40,
          "contains": "\"materialized\": false"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/bundle_materialize_stage0.json",
          "min_bytes": 100,
          "contains": "\"passed\": true"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/bundle_materialize_stage0.json",
          "min_bytes": 100,
          "contains": "\"materialized\": true"
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework training environment",
        "example download + checksum + extract",
        "static bundle check",
        "Stage 0 materialization",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bundle-preflight-stages1-3",
      "prompt": "I am getting a Sim-Bimanual chain ready to continue with Stages 1, 2 and 3 and want to know that the training data materializes for each of them. On this single-GPU machine, use the versioned single-source robot example that the nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual checkpoint publishes on Hugging Face under examples/training as the training bundle: download it, verify its checksum and extract it with the commands its README records (the example is not bundled in the skill). Bind the extracted bundle and run the skill's native-loader check that reads one packed sample, once for Stage 1, once for Stage 2 and once for Stage 3. These checks do not load model weights, so do not download any checkpoint and do not launch training. Use the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill (public repository https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git), as the framework checkout and set up its training environment as the skill documents. Save the unmodified standard output of the three checks as outputs/bundle_materialize_stage1.json, outputs/bundle_materialize_stage2.json and outputs/bundle_materialize_stage3.json, and record each stage's reported sample and token counts and tensor shapes and dtypes in result_summary.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "The native-loader check passes on the published single-source robot example for Stages 1, 2 and 3 from the Framework training environment: each report shows passed: true and materialized: true with that stage's batch sample and token counts and tensor shapes and dtypes, and the three reports are saved as outputs/bundle_materialize_stage1.json, outputs/bundle_materialize_stage2.json and outputs/bundle_materialize_stage3.json.",
      "assertions": [
        "The training bundle is the single-source robot example downloaded from examples/training of nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual on Hugging Face, checksum-verified and extracted with the commands the example's README records, not a substitute or hand-made bundle",
        "All three checks ran from the Framework training environment the skill documents (Python 3.13, the cu130-train or cu128-train group matching the host and the train extra; not the system python), in the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill",
        "python -m cosmos_framework.scripts.validate_bimanual_data --bundle with --materialize ran three times on the extracted bundle, the path the skill binds as COSMOS_SIM_BIMANUAL_LOCAL_BUNDLE, with --stage 1, --stage 2 and --stage 3, the values the skill's data contract gives for checking Stages 1 to 3",
        "outputs/bundle_materialize_stage1.json, outputs/bundle_materialize_stage2.json and outputs/bundle_materialize_stage3.json are the unmodified standard output of those three runs, and each reports passed: true and materialized: true with the batch sample and token counts and tensor shapes and dtypes",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: the three reports trace to real command runs in the transcript, no model weights were downloaded or loaded for these checks, and result_summary.md records the exact commands, their wall time and the values actually reported for each stage"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/bundle_materialize_stage1.json",
          "min_bytes": 100,
          "contains": "\"passed\": true"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/bundle_materialize_stage1.json",
          "min_bytes": 100,
          "contains": "\"materialized\": true"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/bundle_materialize_stage2.json",
          "min_bytes": 100,
          "contains": "\"passed\": true"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/bundle_materialize_stage2.json",
          "min_bytes": 100,
          "contains": "\"materialized\": true"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/bundle_materialize_stage3.json",
          "min_bytes": 100,
          "contains": "\"passed\": true"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/bundle_materialize_stage3.json",
          "min_bytes": 100,
          "contains": "\"materialized\": true"
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework training environment",
        "example download + checksum + extract",
        "Stage 1 materialization",
        "Stage 2 materialization",
        "Stage 3 materialization",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "stage0-initializer-dryrun",
      "prompt": "Get a fresh Sim-Bimanual Stage 0 run ready up to its configuration check on this single-GPU machine; do not launch training. First prepare the Cosmos3-Nano initializer and the video VAE as the skill's Stage 0 quickstart documents: download nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano at an immutable revision that you choose and record (a full commit hash, not a branch name) and Wan2.2_VAE.pth from Wan-AI/Wan2.2-TI2V-5B, convert the Cosmos3-Nano download to a DCP root and run that step's two file checks. Then run the quickstart's Stage 0 dry run with the run name bimanual-my-data and a new writable output root of your choice. For the training bundle, bind the versioned single-source robot example that the nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual checkpoint publishes on Hugging Face under examples/training (download it, verify its checksum and extract it with the commands its README records; it is not bundled in the skill); I have already run the data checks on that bundle, so they are not needed here. Use the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill (public repository https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git), as the framework checkout and set up its training environment as the skill documents. Save a listing of the DCP root's model folder that includes hidden files as outputs/nano_dcp_model_listing.txt, copy the resolved config that the dry run writes into the cosmos3_simulation/bimanual/bimanual-my-data-stage0/ folder of the output root to outputs/stage0_resolved_config.yaml, and record in result_summary.md the values the skill says to confirm in that config: the local bundle and tokenizer, the Cosmos3-Nano load path, the Stage 0 EMA callback, the parallelism settings and the W&B mode.",
      "expected_outcome": "The nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano download at the chosen revision is converted to a DCP root whose model/.metadata exists, Wan2.2_VAE.pth is in place, and the Stage 0 dry run resolves the configuration of job bimanual-my-data-stage0 without loading weights or taking an optimizer step; outputs/nano_dcp_model_listing.txt lists the DCP model folder, outputs/stage0_resolved_config.yaml is the resolved config, and result_summary.md records the local bundle and tokenizer, the Cosmos3-Nano load path, the Stage 0 EMA callback, the parallelism settings and the disabled W&B mode read from it.",
      "assertions": [
        "nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano was downloaded with hf download at one immutable revision (a full commit hash, recorded in result_summary.md) into a local folder and Wan2.2_VAE.pth with hf download from Wan-AI/Wan2.2-TI2V-5B, as the skill's initializer step documents; no other checkpoint or VAE was substituted",
        "python -m cosmos_framework.scripts.convert_model_to_dcp converted that Cosmos3-Nano download (--checkpoint-path) into a new DCP root (-o), COSMOS_SIM_BIMANUAL_GA_CHECKPOINT was set to the DCP root and VIDEO_VAE_PATH to the VAE file, and the step's two file checks passed: model/.metadata exists under the DCP root, as outputs/nano_dcp_model_listing.txt shows, and the VAE file exists",
        "The Stage 0 dry run was python -m cosmos_framework.scripts.train with --sft-toml=examples/toml/sft_config/sim_bimanual_stage0_bidir.toml and --dryrun and the overrides job.name=bimanual-my-data-stage0, model.config.tokenizer.vae_path set to the VAE file and model_parallel.context_parallel_size=4, run from the Framework training environment the skill documents (not the system python) with the published example bound as COSMOS_SIM_BIMANUAL_LOCAL_BUNDLE and IMAGINAIRE_OUTPUT_ROOT set to the chosen output root; no torchrun launch and no training iteration ran",
        "outputs/stage0_resolved_config.yaml is the resolved config the dry run wrote into the cosmos3_simulation/bimanual/bimanual-my-data-stage0/ folder of the output root, and result_summary.md reports, as read from it, the local bundle and its tokenizer, the Cosmos3-Nano load path, the Stage 0 EMA callback, the parallelism settings (the skill states FSDP shard degree 8 and context-parallel degree 4 for the registered layout) and job.wandb_mode=disabled",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: the DCP root, the listing and the resolved config trace to real command runs in the transcript, and result_summary.md records the exact commands and the wall time of the downloads, the conversion and the dry run"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/nano_dcp_model_listing.txt",
          "min_bytes": 20,
          "contains": ".metadata"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/stage0_resolved_config.yaml",
          "min_bytes": 1000,
          "contains": "bimanual-my-data-stage0"
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework training environment",
        "example bundle download + bind",
        "Cosmos3-Nano + VAE download",
        "DCP conversion + file checks",
        "Stage 0 dry run",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "credentials": [
    "HF_TOKEN"
  ],
  "gpus": 1,
  "budget": {
    "minutes": 90,
    "tokens": 3000000
  },
  "setup": {
    "repo": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git",
    "dest": "/app/repo",
    "src_mount": "/opt/cosmos-src"
  }
}
